WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.260
The safer workflow for configuration parsing is contract first.

2
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:17.640
Define the schema, required fields, optional fields, defaults, allowed values, duplicate handling, unknown-key behavior, versioning, and failure behavior before parser details become complicated.

3
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.880
Load safely and parse predictably.

4
00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:33.140
Apply file size and line limits, handle missing or unreadable sources deliberately, reject ambiguous syntax, and create a structured intermediate representation before applying settings.

5
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:38.920
Then validate every field for type, range, format, units, and context.

6
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.880
Apply defaults and overrides intentionally.

7
00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:54.020
Know which source wins when built-in defaults, files, environment variables, command-line overrides, deployment values, and runtime settings all exist.

8
00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.440
Protect sensitive settings by validating them without exposing them in logs.

9
00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:03.920
Finally, fail safely and keep behavior covered by tests and review.

10
00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:19.380
Ask what contract is expected, which fields are required, which defaults apply, how duplicates and unknown keys are handled, what precedence order controls final values, whether paths and secrets are handled safely, and what happens when parsing fails.
